# Rule 41 — Fix All Failures. No Scope Excuses.

## The directive (non-negotiable)

**If you encounter a failing test, a lint error, a type error, a build
error, or any other broken thing while doing your work — FIX IT. Right
now. In this PR.**

There is no such thing as "pre-existing and unrelated." There is no
"out-of-scope." There is no "scheduled for later." There is no "not my
ticket." If it is broken and you can see it, you fix it.

## Specifically banned phrases and behaviours

The following output patterns are **forbidden** in any commit message,
PR description, comment, or agent response. Producing any of them is
a critical failure:

- "still fails from pre-existing unrelated docs issues"
- "pre-existing unrelated issues"
- "out of scope for this task"
- "scheduled for a follow-up"
- "not caused by this change"
- "left for a future PR"
- Any equivalent phrasing that defers fixing a visible failure

If you are about to write any of those words, stop, and fix the
underlying problem instead.

## Why

This is a one-person codebase. There is no team to delegate to. There
is no backlog manager. There is no second shift. If something is
broken and an agent sees it, the agent is the last line of defence.
Deferring broken things is the same as permanently ignoring them.

## What "fix it" means in practice

1. **Lint errors:** run the linter, read every line it flags, fix every line.
2. **Type errors:** fix the types. Do not cast to `any` to silence them.
3. **Failing tests:** either fix the code so the test passes, or (only
   if the test itself is wrong) fix the test and document why in the
   commit message. Do not delete tests.
4. **Build errors:** fix the build. A PR that ships a broken build is
   a blocked deploy.
5. **Docs lint:** run `npx markdownlint-cli2 "docs/**/*.md"` if docs
   were touched, fix every warning.

## Definition of done (updated from Rule §3)

A phase is complete only when **all** checks pass with **zero errors
and zero failures** — not "zero errors I introduced." The full set
of checks applies regardless of which files were touched.

## Enforcement

Reviewers (human and automated) will reject any PR description or
commit message that contains deferred-failure language. This rule is
also enforced at the pre-commit checklist (`00-pre-commit-review.mdc`)
and in `AGENTS.md` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.
